# index1 — a secondary index with sets
#
# Learn: Redis looks things up by key only. To find "users in Paris" you
# keep your own index: a set per value (idx:user:city:paris holds the ids
# of Parisians) that you update together with the record, inside
# MULTI/EXEC so nobody sees one without the other. SMOVE moves a member
# between two sets atomically.
#
# Task: the check seeds users 1-3 and their city index. Inside ONE
# transaction:
#   - add user 4 (name Lin, city paris) and index them,
#   - user 2 moved from paris to lyon: update the hash AND the index.
# Then print the members of the paris index.
#

MULTI
HSET user:4 name Lin city paris
HSET user:2 city lyon
EXEC
SMEMBERS idx:user:city:paris
